[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#2C3E50]LeafRTP[/COLOR][COLOR=#2980B9]-Pro[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#555555]High-Performance Random Teleport (RTP) Plugin for Folia, Paper & Spigot[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[CENTER][I]Once upon a time, I wanted to explore a minecraft world. I asked for [/I]/rtp[I] in servers I played on. They told me "no, that's laggy", and I took that personally.[/I][/CENTER]

Most random-teleport plugins pick a coordinate, load the chunk on the main thread, and - if the spot turns out unsafe - pick another, with no bound on the retries. The cost lands in MSPT: one [I]/rtp[/I] can hold the tick loop for hundreds of milliseconds while every other player waits. A menu sits on top of that; the engine underneath is what decides the tick cost.

[B]LeafRTP-Pro is built so that a teleport costs the server nothing a player can feel.[/B]

On Paper: 19.8 TP/s sustained at a 4 ms worst-case main-thread tick, where the next-best plugin needs 70 ms. On Folia: 13.5 TP/s with zero region watchdog stalls, on a run where the next plugin froze a region for over 20 seconds. Four safety prohibitions - no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silently dropped failures - are enforced by build rules that fail the build when code violates them. The harness is in the repo and the quality gates are listed below with their thresholds.

[CENTER][I]Supported: Paper, Folia, Spigot, Fabric, and native NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x) - Minecraft 1.20.x / 1.21.x / 26.x. Legacy Forge is not native: run the Spigot/Paper jar under Arclight / Mohist. Defaults are usable without tuning; every tunable is exposed in YAML. Drop-in upgrade from the free LeafRTP build.[/I][/CENTER]
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why operators pick Pro[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[CENTER][SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#27AE60]19.8 TP/s on Paper at 4 ms worst-case tick. 13.5 TP/s on Folia, zero region stalls.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

LeafRTP-Pro is a polygon-bounded, Folia-native random teleport engine for high-load and custom-world Minecraft servers. If [I]/rtp[/I] is the top entry in your timings report, this is what it addresses:

[LIST]
[*][B]No lag spikes when players spam [I]/rtp[/I].[/B] Worst-case main-thread tick stays at 4 ms (vs. 70-771 ms for the next plugins) - your TPS holds at 20.00 during a teleport burst.
[*][B]Instant teleports, no "Finding a safe location..." wait.[/B] Pre-verified location queue serves [I]/rtp[/I] in one tick instead of loading chunks on demand.
[*][B]Runs natively on Folia without stalling regions.[/B] Under an identical 3-client burst, LeafRTP-Pro sustained 13.5 TP/s at 100% success with zero Folia watchdog stalls and just 3.96 ms of main-thread cost per teleport, while EzRTP managed 5.3 TP/s and blocked region threads on synchronous chunk loads - tripping the Folia watchdog 7 times, one region frozen for over 20 seconds.
[*][B]No tuning required on install.[/B] Pre-warmed location queue, persistent spatial memory, off-tick Anvil pre-filter, and async chunk loading are all active at first start. The [I]config.yml[/I], commands, and claim-plugin integrations (GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect) are the same as the free build, so the upgrade needs no config migration.
[*][B]Safety prohibitions enforced at build time.[/B] No unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silent failures. Each prohibition has an ArchUnit rule that fails the build if code violates it - see the Quality metrics section below.
[/LIST]

