Pro is the early-access tier: tuned versions of new platforms and scaling backends land here first, because each one carries a hands-on support burden that is only guaranteed on the paid tier. The free build runs on Folia (basic regionized scheduling + async teleport) and supports cross-server moves via plugin-messaging (backends behind a proxy); Pro's tuned Folia adapter and durable SQL/Redis transports graduate to the free build once stabilized. Configuration, data files, and commands are identical between the builds, so the upgrade is drop-in.
 
[SIZE=2][I]* BungeeCord proxy adapter is planned; currently supported via plugin-messaging on the backend.[/I][/SIZE]
 
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Built for[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
LeafRTP-Pro runs on any server. The setups below are where the difference in tick cost is largest:

[LIST]
[*][B]High-concurrency servers[/B] where /rtp spam used to spike MSPT and shake TPS.
[*][B]Folia deployments[/B] that need region-aware scheduling and zero foreign-region API hops in the teleport hot path.
[*][B]Multi-server networks (Velocity)[/B] that need cross-network LeafRTP with reservation tokens and shared state. Validated on the in-repo devstack: [B]2 Velocity proxies, 2 lobby servers, 2 backend servers[/B] behind a shared Redis transport.
[*][B]Large or pregenerated worlds[/B] where chunk-load cost dominates - the pre-validated queue and Anvil pre-filter take that cost off the teleport path.
[*][B]Custom-generator worlds (Iris, Terra, datapacks)[/B] where the Anvil-first biome read keeps your safety config authoritative across MC upgrades.
[*][B]Either operator style.[/B] Defaults out of the box, or version-controlled YAML and profiler output. The in-game [I]/rtp menu[/I] is optional; every action it exposes is also a typed command.
[/LIST]

[B]Platform requirements:[/B] Java 21+, on Paper / Folia / Spigot / Fabric / native NeoForge. Legacy Forge is not native - run the Spigot/Paper jar under Arclight / Mohist.

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

