[I]On Folia, LeafRTP's main-thread cost per teleport drops to ~4 ms as region threads parallelize work Paper serializes onto one tick thread. EzRTP's 7 watchdog stalls (one region unresponsive 20.4 s) are the server's own record of synchronous [/I]World.loadChunk[I] calls on region threads; LeafRTP issued none. The free build cleared the same run at 12.5 TP/s with zero stalls: the shared [/I]rtp-core[I] engine carries the Folia result, not a Pro-only adapter. The gap between the two editions is 1.0 TP/s at 3 clients and has not been measured under heavier per-region contention.[/I]

